{"title":"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The perimeter of an equilateral triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/a/27acd04b639e953161234b726233dd34257cbf3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15 \\text{ m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"39\" height=\"14\" />. What is the length of each side of the triangle?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/9/9798527c729a2c398a76187699508909ab25471b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 7.5 \\text{ m} \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 5 \\text{ m} \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 3.75 \\text{ m} \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 10 \\text{ m} \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 17 \\text{ m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"503\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Because all three sides of an <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Equilateral_triangle\" title=\"Equilateral triangle\">equilateral triangle</a> are equal, the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Perimeter\" title=\"Perimeter\">perimeter</a> of an equilateral triangle is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times its side length. This means that the side length of the equilateral triangle with perimeter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/a/27acd04b639e953161234b726233dd34257cbf3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15 \\text{ m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"39\" height=\"14\" /> would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/0/a40db3d86a7b353b5bda8ee3094ddec4a1f17767.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{15}{3} = \\boxed{\\textbf {(B) } 5 \\text{ m}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"123\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(G